I promise I'll...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.520
I won't put them on the wire till tomorrow.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:02.960
Well, I guess you rate that.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:04.230
For effort, anyway.

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:06.620
Barton, take my seams to Ludlow.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.160
And I hope you have a strong stomach.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:16.330
We're going to take some pictures in Ludlow.

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:18.830
If we're not back in 15 minutes,

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.120
better come in after us.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:20.960
Yes, sir.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:22.040
Let him through.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:07.610
I've had enough. Some people use calendars to tell age.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:10.350
I could use ruins to count mine.

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.730
I was 25 when I went through Seoul after it was shelled.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:19.580
20 when I took my camera into Cologne and Berlin after World War II.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:22.320
Must be used to it by now.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:27.100
Captain, there are some things you never get used to.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:36.700
How about a drink to wipe away some memories?

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:38.770
Good way to get rid of the jitters.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:40.240
I know a little place...

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:43.160
How do 150 people vanish into thin air?

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.200
Well, around this part of the country,

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.840
things seem to have a way of vanishing.

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.570
Only a couple of months ago, it was a warehouse.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.930
Kind of fell apart overnight, just like Ludlow.

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:20.810
Frank if you decide to come back and do a story on us well no as a matter of fact I came back for

