01:02:54.220 --> 01:02:57.300
Why didn't you put the oscillator in the boat in the first place to send out the call?

01:02:57.820 --> 01:02:58.800
Why track them here?

01:02:59.290 --> 01:02:59.970
Because we'd never...

01:03:01.650 --> 01:03:06.240
Here, look. Here we are in downtown Chicago, near the lake.

01:03:06.900 --> 01:03:09.940
Now, the locusts are scattered all through the suburbs and on the south side.

01:03:10.600 --> 01:03:12.220
Now, we'll send out the call from here.

01:03:12.320 --> 01:03:14.540
Yes, but that's going to attract them to us, not into the water.

01:03:14.930 --> 01:03:18.450
Well, first of all, it's imperative that every last one of the locusts hear the call.

01:03:18.750 --> 01:03:21.270
Now, in order to do that, we've got to get our amplifier speaker

01:03:21.270 --> 01:03:23.730
at the highest possible point to get maximum range.

01:03:24.140 --> 01:03:26.020
Now, we've got ours on the roof of this building,

01:03:26.120 --> 01:03:27.580
which is one of the tallest in Chicago.

01:03:28.060 --> 01:03:29.510
Now, once we get them here...

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:31.300
I see. Then the boat will take over.

01:03:31.480 --> 01:03:34.580
Exactly. Once we have them in the heart of the loop, near our location,

01:03:34.740 --> 01:03:36.920
they'll be within range of the amplifier on the boat.

01:03:37.570 --> 01:03:40.450
Now, we'll then radio our oscillator signal out to the boat,

01:03:40.850 --> 01:03:43.590
and they, in turn, will rebroadcast it over their amplifier,

01:03:44.460 --> 01:03:48.000
attracting the locusts to them and into the lake.

01:03:49.370 --> 01:03:51.830
We hope. We hope.

01:03:53.730 --> 01:03:55.470
Now, will you check and see about the temperature?

01:03:58.470 --> 01:03:59.430
How can we be sure, sir?

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:01.040
What do you mean?

01:04:01.740 --> 01:04:03.200
How can you know that we'll get them all?

01:04:03.860 --> 01:04:07.000
Well, that's where our observation posts and the helicopter come in.

01:04:07.280 --> 01:04:10.660
From their reports, we'll know the exact location of the locusts at all times,

01:04:11.440 --> 01:04:12.580
and if it's working.

01:04:14.640 --> 01:04:18.060
70 degrees, Ed. They're probably starting to move.

01:04:19.400 --> 01:04:21.300
Emergency lab to all observation posts.

01:04:21.480 --> 01:04:23.500
Emergency lab to all observation posts.

01:04:23.700 --> 01:04:24.300
Report in.

01:04:27.060 --> 01:04:29.540
Observation post number two to emergency lab, over.

01:04:30.540 --> 01:04:31.760
What is your location? Over.

01:04:32.260 --> 01:04:36.100
I'm situated in a store across from the Art Institute on Michigan Boulevard.

01:04:36.800 --> 01:04:39.220
The street is empty. Nothing in sight. Out.

01:04:40.380 --> 01:04:42.560
Observation post number three to emergency lab.

01:04:43.070 --> 01:04:44.590
I'm on the roof of the Drayton Hotel.

01:04:45.780 --> 01:04:49.340
Don't see any grasshoppers in this area, but the south side's getting some action.

01:04:50.350 --> 01:04:50.630
Out.

01:04:51.330 --> 01:04:53.070
Emergency lab to observation post one.

01:04:53.460 --> 01:04:55.540
Emergency lab to observation post one.

01:04:56.100 --> 01:04:57.240
You did not report in.

01:04:58.040 --> 01:04:59.500
What's your location, post one?

01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:02.060
This is observation post number one.

01:05:02.360 --> 01:05:03.520
I'm right in the middle of them.

01:05:03.940 --> 01:05:06.440
I'm just south of 73rd and South Shore Drive.

01:05:06.850 --> 01:05:07.230
Out.

01:05:10.090 --> 01:05:11.230
Emergency lab to helicopter.

01:05:11.490 --> 01:05:11.690
Over.

01:05:14.630 --> 01:05:16.010
Helicopter to emergency lab.

01:05:16.620 --> 01:05:19.100
The locusts are active on the south side of Chicago.

01:05:19.590 --> 01:05:21.610
As yet there are none in the downtown area.

01:05:21.910 --> 01:05:22.230
Out.

01:05:22.750 --> 01:05:24.170
Can you read me emergency lab?

01:05:24.900 --> 01:05:25.160
Over.

01:05:25.970 --> 01:05:27.130
Yes, we can read you fine, General.

01:05:27.290 --> 01:05:27.930
Are you all set?

01:05:28.150 --> 01:05:28.410
Over.

01:05:30.380 --> 01:05:31.600
We're not quite ready yet.

01:05:32.380 --> 01:05:34.340
I think you better hold off a few more minutes.

01:05:35.530 --> 01:05:35.850
Over.

01:05:36.850 --> 01:05:38.290
I think we better start now, General.

01:05:38.730 --> 01:05:42.250
If they should change their direction and start moving away from Chicago, we may not get them all.

01:05:42.470 --> 01:05:42.790
Over.

01:05:43.010 --> 01:05:46.530
I think you're starting until we're completely ready.

01:05:46.750 --> 01:05:50.210
This boat has to draw them away from you at a split second's notice.

01:05:51.340 --> 01:05:51.700
Over.

01:05:52.500 --> 01:05:53.400
I'd like to start, sir.

01:05:55.810 --> 01:05:56.450
Then go ahead.

01:06:03.480 --> 01:06:08.540
Sergeant. Yes, sir. Is that the wire that leads to the speaker on the roof?

01:06:08.900 --> 01:06:10.940
Yes, sir. Oh, plug it into the amplifier, will you?

01:06:11.080 --> 01:06:11.560
Yes, sir.

01:06:29.460 --> 01:06:29.980
Post number one.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:34.340
to emergency lab. The locusts are leaving this section. They're heading towards Chicago's downtown.

01:06:37.760 --> 01:06:42.140
